CONCLUSION: WHY THIS MATTERS
================================================================================

FOR THE BANK:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

• Less money lost to fraud (saves millions)
• Happier customers (fewer false alarms)
• Better compliance (avoids fines)
• Competitive advantage (better security than other banks)

FOR THE ACCOUNTANT:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

• Less boring manual work (focus on interesting investigations)
• Better tools (make decisions with confidence)
• Career growth (learn modern banking systems)
• Less stress (system helps, doesn't replace)

FOR THE CUSTOMERS:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

• Safer money (better fraud protection)
• Faster service (quicker problem resolution)
• Better experience (fewer unnecessary account freezes)

FOR SOCIETY:
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

• Less crime (criminals have harder time)
• More trust (people trust banks more)
• Economic stability (banking system more secure)

